  "id": "unconscious-process",
  "term": "unconscious process",
  "definition": "An unconscious process is a mental way a person or group uses, outside awareness, to cope with impulses, feelings, or ideas that are not acceptable at the conscious level. It refers to defensive mental activity such as projection, reaction formation, or self-reversal.",
